<title>UK: Newcastle United to float despite loss of Keegan.</title>
<headline>Newcastle United to float despite loss of Keegan.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>English Premier League soccer club Newcastle United will press ahead with its planned flotation despite the shock resignation of manager Kevin Keegan, a club spokesman said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;This doesn't alter the float timetable,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Newcastle last month confirmed plans to join the London Stock Exchange this spring and said further details of the listing would be made available in mid-January.</p>
<p>A further announcement is expected next week on the flotation of the club owned by property magnate Sir John Hall. Analysts say it is likely to be valued at over 150 million stg.</p>
</text>
